        "details": "Brahmā directs Dakṣa to worship Śakti so she becomes his daughter. After100 years Śakti appears; Dakṣa hymns her as māyā/delusion, mother/life-giver, Pārvatī/Gāyatrī/Sāvitrī/Prakṛti/Puruṣa and guṇa support, requesting daughterhood. She grants future daughterhood in many forms and filling the world through offspring, promises her hymn’s readers/hearers all wishes, and vanishes. Mudgala then addresses current Dakṣa: he abandoned Gaṇeśa name/mantra, scorned Satī who became ash, was made sorrowful by Vighneśa, but prior impressions restored memory. Kingship prosperity induces proud blindness/destroys knowledge, so sages avoid it; hear the present account devotedly.",
